 # BUG REGISTRY
 
+## BUG-009 — Legacy global hidden-action coupling survives after mouse-free transport
+
+- Status: FIXED-IN-SOURCE / BUILD + RUNTIME PENDING
+- Severity: High multi-client isolation
+- First observed: architecture review of v0.6.1.5
+- Related features: SELL, trade, REC, P1/P2/P3 scheduler
+- Evidence: EVID-013
+
+### Root cause and fix
+
+v0.6.1.5 removed Windows mouse injection but retained coordinator busy/owner/sequence/recording concepts inherited from a shared physical input resource. v0.6.1.6 removes global input ownership, scopes recorder state, removes SELL→trade blocking, makes priority local per account and retains only a business Trade Workflow Lock for the active MAIN↔CON transaction.
+
+## BUG-008 — First Mount can bypass the AutoFight-OFF Travel Guard
+
+- Status: FIXED-IN-SOURCE / BUILD + RUNTIME PENDING
+- Severity: Critical movement invariant
+- First observed: source review of v0.6.1.5
+- Related feature: robust travel / mount recovery
+- Evidence: EVID-013
+
+### Root cause
+
+The central `SendDecision` path guarded `Action::StartPath`, while the first `Action::Mount` attempt could call the ride action directly. A later retry branch happened to stop AutoFight before remounting, but this did not establish a universal Mount invariant.
+
+### Fix in v0.6.1.6
+
+The central action gate now handles `Action::Mount || Action::StartPath` identically: conflict latch must be clear and `EnsureAutoFightOffForTravel` must prove a fresh authoritative AutoFight OFF snapshot before either movement action can dispatch.
+
