 # DECISION REGISTRY
 
+## DEC-007 — Per-client action ownership and one common movement gate
+
+- Date/version: 2026-08-21 / v0.6.1.6
+- Status: ACTIVE / BUILD + RUNTIME PENDING
+- Decision: remove global input ownership between clients; retain only locks that protect business state inside a client or active MAIN↔CON transaction. Both Mount and StartPath must pass the same authoritative AutoFight-OFF guard.
+
+### Why
+
+Internal InputSync actions target a specific client and do not consume a shared Windows cursor, so a global input lease creates needless coupling. However, transaction order, recorder scope and one-client UI mutation are still real correctness constraints. The first Mount path also exposed a gap: StartPath was guarded while Mount itself could be sent before AutoFight was proven OFF.
+
+### Constraints
+
+- No global hidden-action busy/owner state.
+- Trade Workflow Lock is business-only and cannot block an unrelated PID's point action.
+- SELL on one PID cannot globally pause trade on another PID.
+- Recorder blocks only the PID/pair whose manual coordinates are being captured.
+- Evaluate P1→P2→P3 independently per account.
+- Fan out read-only Bridge snapshot polling per PID, but keep UI/profile-mutating FSM work on the controller thread until it is explicitly redesigned for thread safety.
+- Both `Action::Mount` and `Action::StartPath` call the same `EnsureAutoFightOffForTravel`; do not duplicate or weaken the two-stop/reset loop.
+- Client Freeze and F4 remain valid global/safety behavior and are not removed merely because mouse serialization disappeared.
+
